   "design": "Approved web pages answer routine questions on licences, rules and opening hours. The shelter's impound records are linked to the lost-and-found pet register, so callers check reported and found pets themselves and the officer finds them in one search. A searchable procedure page replaces looking up ordinances in documents. Call notes go into the case register, so the spreadsheet log ends. Answering people in person, by phone and by mail, and writing notes, stay with the officer. No chatbot is used.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "Every routine question came by phone and records were searched one by one.",
   "enabler_now": "Approved web pages and a lost-and-found register linked to shelter records.",
   "still_hard": "Callers in distress about a missing or injured animal.",
   "human_edge": "Calming an owner whose dog was impounded.",
